  engineer> Can we roll back to 4.2 if it goes badly?

  agent> Buffered telemetry written under 5.x is NOT readable after rolling back to 4.3. [RB-107#1] To replace: power down, remove the four M3 screws on the underside, disconnect the u.FL pigtail gently — it tears if pulled sideways — and lift the radio daughterboard straight up. [RB-101#1] A device that has already expired cannot rotate over the air — it can no longer establish the TLS session needed to fetch the new certificate. [RB-104#1] Fit the replacement, torque the screws to 0.4 Nm, and re-pair with `helios-cli radio pair --site <id>`. [RB-101#1]

